Subject: [202605] Keep Edgecore thermal control alive through missing sensor reads

AS7326 boot logs show None * 1000 killing the fan loop after its initial
38 percent setting. Apply explicit missing/nonfinite sensor handling to
AS7326, AS7726 and AS7816 PDDF loops and AS5835 native fan control.
Keep global fan PWM at 100 percent while a required reading is unavailable,
retry in the existing loop, then resume each model's existing thermal
policy. Start PDDF loops at full speed until valid readings are available.
Restart unexpected service failures instead of leaving control dead.
AS7726 accepts both vendor uppercase and standard lowercase direction
strings, retaining its distinct airflow policies; no thresholds change.
Reference: Edgecore thermal implementations at d39662e9; these still
have unguarded sensor reads, so this is a local recovery fix.

Verified source: 5ef9e45ccf7f004fb07bf3f9be2f471cf00573bf.
Remove individual fixes when upstream supplies equivalent behavior.
Software regressions cover these changes; only AS7326 has been
inspected live. Other models require installation/hardware validation.

